    <string name="guide_title">HOW NACE AUTOMATION WORKS</string>
    <string name="guide_intro">You are all set. Please read these points once. You can open this guide again from Settings.</string>
    <string name="guide_1">Make sure the correct currency is selected: BTC or ETH. The highlighted (orange) one is the one NACE Automation will trade.</string>
    <string name="guide_2">NACE Automation trades in 3 time windows a day. If you have more trade windows, add them with %1$s.</string>
    <string name="guide_3">%1$s shows the trade live, as it happens. It does not interrupt NACE Automation.</string>
    <string name="guide_4">CONTROL lets you use the NACE website yourself, as in a browser. NACE Automation is OFF while CONTROL is open, so close it when you are done.</string>
    <string name="guide_5">When the app shows these signs in green, NACE Automation is ready and the trade will be made:</string>
    <string name="guide_6">If NACE Automation is not ready for a trade, you are warned with sounds, a spoken warning and a notification. If this happens, open the app and follow the instructions to fix it.</string>
    <string name="guide_7">You cannot be signed in to your NACE account in this app and in a browser at the same time. To withdraw or check your account, use the CONTROL button instead of a browser.</string>
    <string name="guide_8">Keep the phone charged and connected to the internet at trade times. Do not force-close NACE Automation or swipe it away from recent apps: it has to keep running in the background.</string>
    <string name="guide_9">About 5 minutes before each trade, NACE Automation says \"NACE automation online. Waiting for the trade.\" After the trade, it says the result.</string>
    <string name="guide_10">In Settings (gear icon) you can stop NACE Automation, turn alert sounds off, or open this guide again.</string>
